 "source": ";; let / let* / letrec / named let. Named let is the same `let` head as\n;; the unnamed one; emacs scheme-let-indent looks at whether the cadr is\n;; a symbol. Both are a `list` node.\n(define (plain-let x)\n(let ((a 1)\n(b 2))\n(+ a b x)))\n\n(define (star-let x)\n(let* ((a x)\n(b (+ a 1)))\nb))\n\n(define (rec-let n)\n(letrec ((even?\n(lambda (x)\n(if (zero? x) #t (odd? (- x 1)))))\n(odd?\n(lambda (x)\n(if (zero? x) #f (even? (- x 1))))))\n(even? n)))\n\n(define (named-sum n) ; named let: cadr is a symbol, so specform 2\n(let loop ((i 0)\n(acc 0))\n(if (= i n)\nacc\n(loop (+ i 1) (+ acc i)))))\n",
